WEBVTT

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.769
Inlooveu. A university social platform I built
and launched.

00:00:06.099 --> 00:00:09.715
First, email and password, with validation.

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:15.565
Next come personal details, degree information
and discovery preferences.

00:00:18.099 --> 00:00:21.484
The form also includes photos, a description
and interests.

00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:24.723
This walkthrough stops before the final
submission.

00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:30.710
A profile brings that introduction together:
photos, a description and interests.

00:00:31.558 --> 00:00:35.891
We can explore and edit how a person
introduces themselves.

00:00:38.099 --> 00:00:40.781
Photos take the lead on the main screen.

00:00:41.629 --> 00:00:44.772
Each card opens a profile and introduces the
person.

00:00:47.099 --> 00:00:50.266
In the profile detail, we read the description
and interests.

00:00:51.114 --> 00:00:54.148
The personal introduction accompanies the
photos.

00:00:57.099 --> 00:01:04.706
The gallery lets us browse several profile
photos. These cards use actual photos and
profile data from the Inlooveu backup.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.793
The swipe visibly moves the card.

00:01:09.641 --> 00:01:11.498
A like or a dismissal records the decision;

00:01:11.765 --> 00:01:14.386
a mutual like is detected.

00:01:16.099 --> 00:01:18.380
The chat stays visible in two windows.

00:01:19.228 --> 00:01:22.711
We send a message from one account and see it
appear in the other.

00:01:23.561 --> 00:01:25.672
The API saves the message in MongoDB

00:01:25.684 --> 00:01:28.160
before distributing the record through
Socket.IO.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.583
The exchange continues from both clients.

00:01:36.091 --> 00:01:39.337
After a reload, the API retrieves history from
MongoDB.

00:01:40.124 --> 00:01:43.020
The messages remain available when we return
to the conversation.

00:01:44.099 --> 00:01:45.907
React and TypeScript on the client.

00:01:46.755 --> 00:01:50.189
Express, MongoDB and Socket.IO connect
persistence

00:01:50.201 --> 00:01:51.706
with real-time events.

00:01:54.099 --> 00:01:58.369
Pierre Burciaga. Explore the product and
engineering decisions.
